LAMMPS (4 Jul 2026 - Development - patch_4Jul2026-542-g4e5eb25ab6-modified)
  using 1 OpenMP thread(s) per MPI task
# 13,216-atom Cu/ZnCl2(aq) cell in the conductor mode: each copper electrode is one fragment (molecule 90001, 90002)
# carrying the Gaussian self-energy (width 0.5 A); no eigenvalue ridge. Otherwise identical to in.cucell_bench.
# Benchmark deck for proc-grid optimization: reads data.cell_L0, steady 300 K, short run.
# Same physics/cost as the production relax/equil (FQ solve + rexpon + EAM + SHAKE), with the load
# balance the inhomogeneous slab+vacuum cell needs.  Reports Loop time / Performance (timesteps/s).
#   run: srun ... lmp_cpu -in in.cucell_bench -var NB 500 [-var GRID "* * 1"]
variable        NB     index 500
variable        RIDGE  index 69.1815
units           real
atom_style      full
boundary        p p p
comm_style      tiled                     # slab+vacuum -> RCB load balance
if "${GRID} != none" then "processors ${GRID}"
special_bonds   lj/coul 1.0e-8 1.0e-8 1.0
read_data       data.cell_L0_conductor.data extra/special/per/atom 2
